<section class="content-section" id="disclaimer-claimer">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <div class="feature-card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--gold-primary);">
            <p style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.3em; color: var(--gold-dim); text-transform: uppercase;">
                An Important &ldquo;Claimer&rdquo;
            </p>
        </div>
        <p style="font-style: italic; opacity: 0.85;">
            What follows was written by Brother Aaron Powner and his brother Jim Powner when
            Words of Plainness was first published. It remains the founding posture of this
            ministry.
        </p>
        <p>
            The word &ldquo;disclaimer&rdquo; is such a strange term to use. It means that
            you claim that you do not claim something. To disclaim is not the intent of this
            publication. We intend to both claim and proclaim our faith, practices, beliefs,
            and experiences as followers of Jesus Christ in the Latter-day Saint tradition.
        </p>
        <p>
            We are regular, every-day followers of the Latter-day Saint faith. Not being
            guiding officers of the Church to which we have united ourselves, we humbly
            acknowledge that the views expressed in this publication do not necessarily
            reflect the official doctrines, policies, or practices of The Church of Jesus
            Christ of Latter-day Saints or its officials.
        </p>
        <p>
            We are, however, properly ordained elders in the lay-priesthood of our local
            congregations. &ldquo;We talk of Christ, we rejoice in Christ, we preach of
            Christ&hellip; that our children may know to what source they may look for a
            remission of their sins.&rdquo;
            (<a href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/2-ne/25.26" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold">2&nbsp;Nephi&nbsp;25:26</a>)
            We labor to honor the commitment we have made to &ldquo;the work of the
            ministry&rdquo; even to &ldquo;stand as witnesses of God at all times and in all
            things.&rdquo;
            (<a href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/nt/eph/4.12" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold">Ephesians&nbsp;4:12</a>;
            <a href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/bofm/mosiah/18.9" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold">Mosiah&nbsp;18:9</a>)
            Our words do carry the weight of personal conviction and the authenticity of
            individual experiences. We hope you will find within these pages something of
            value.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top: 1.75rem; font-style: italic; opacity: 0.8;">
            What follows below is the legal and administrative companion to that
            claim&mdash;the specific boundaries, trademarks, and terms under which this
            ministry operates.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

